+#if defined(ISHTAR)
+/*
+ * Device SPIs: a driver attaches a handler, the line is set up as Linux's gic-v3 does (Group 1 NS, priority 0xa0,
+ * level or edge, routed to the attaching CPU) and enabled. sleh_irq calls the handler with IRQs masked, then EOIs.
+ * ponytail: one handler per line and no detach; add both when a driver needs them.
